THIS IS MAMBA-1's S6 SELECTIVE SCAN, the kernel behind
mamba_ssm.ops.selective_scan_interface.selective_scan_fn and the one the existing
kernel/cuda/mamba_s6/mamba_s6.cu reimplements.  Mamba-2's SSD and Mamba-3 are Triton
and TileLang, not CUDA, and live in the PyTorch half at
baselines/ssm/upstream/mamba_ssm/ops/.

NOT ONE BYTE WAS CHANGED.  Verify against the archive with `diff -r`.

HOW IT IS BUILT HERE.  Upstream builds these into the `selective_scan_cuda` Python
extension through its own setup.py.  kernel/cuda/mamba_s6/upstream.py builds the
same sources with torch.utils.cpp_extension.load and the same flags setup.py passes,
so no pip install and no touching of the environment's torch is required -- see that
file's header, and see requirements.txt for why `pip install mamba-ssm` is not an
option in this repository.
